<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ibrahim ibn Hajjaj</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died c. 910</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ibrahim ibn Hajjaj was an Arab noble of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seville">Seville</a> who made the city an autonomous lordship during the fitna that shook the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate-of-cordoba">Emirate of Córdoba</a> in the late 9th century. Nominally loyal to the emir, he ruled as an independent prince, kept a court of poets and scholars, and made Seville a cultural rival of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a>.</p></div>
